==English==

{{wikipedia|River Thames}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|Temese|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|Tamesis|lang=la}}, ultimately of {{etyl|cel|en}} origin. The letter ''h'' was mistakenly inserted during the Renaissance, to make the word appear as if it was derived from Greek. The pronunciation, though, did not change to {{IPAchar|/θ/}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|rivers in England and Ontario}} {{enPR|tĕmz}}, {{IPA|/tɛmz/}}
* {{audio|en-uk-Thames.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{audio|en-us-Thames.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{sense|river in Connecticut}} {{IPA|/θeɪmz/}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# [[river|River]] in southern [[England]] flowing 336 [[km]] (209 [[mile|mi.]]) through [[London]] to the [[North Sea]].
# [[river|River]] in [[Ontario]] province, [[Canada]], flowing 258 [[km]] (160 [[mile|mi.]]) to Lake [[St. Clair]].
# [[estuary|Estuary]] in the U.S. State of [[Connecticut]] flowing 24 [[km]] (15 [[mile|mi.]]) past [[New London]] to [[Long Island Sound]].

